# CODEOWNERS
# Defines who is automatically requested to review PRs touching specific paths.
# GitHub enforces this — listed owners must approve before merge (if branch protection is on).
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything not matched below
* @your-org/team-name

# Claude and AI config — reviewed by whoever owns the AI tooling
CLAUDE.md @your-org/team-name
PROJECT_REF.md @your-org/team-name
.claude/ @your-org/team-name
.mcp.json @your-org/team-name

# GitHub Actions and CI — reviewed by whoever owns DevOps
.github/ @your-org/devops

# Security-sensitive files
.env.example @your-org/team-lead
**/auth/** @your-org/team-lead
**/security/** @your-org/team-lead

# Documentation
docs/ @your-org/team-name
*.md @your-org/team-name

# Source code — replace with your actual structure
src/ @your-org/team-name
